WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:07.257
- Growing up they tell us being gay,
you go to hell.

00:00:07.341 --> 00:00:10.177
When my father put my arm
to the flame, he told me,

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.846
"This is what it feels
for 5 seconds.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.389
Imagine eternity."

00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:19.102
-Action.

00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:21.980
-We can all relate to someone
who is coming from a small town

00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:24.149
who is not able
to be himself.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.236
-I play Zain.
He helps Rafiq

00:00:27.319 --> 00:00:29.279
discover a new
way to live his life.

00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:31.990
- Are you not afraid
people will find out?

00:00:32.074 --> 00:00:34.159
- Of course, I'm scared.
That's why I'm going to America.

00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:35.744
I'm going to be
a Hollywood star.

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:38.664
- Rafiq needs to
leave the Middle East.

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:41.750
He is not safe because of
his sexual orientation,

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.837
and he needs to seek asylum.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.715
So many people across the world
have struggled so much

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:51.510
to find a place
where they can be themselves,

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:53.804
and more than that, to, like,
know that they can be loved.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:57.182
- When it comes to artist rights
in Syria, they are persecuted,

00:00:57.266 --> 00:00:59.768
especially when they approach
any freedom issues.

00:00:59.852 --> 00:01:02.938
I believe that this project
comes as a response.

00:01:03.021 --> 00:01:06.275
This is the first show about
LGBTQ rights in Syria,

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:08.861
and it opens a new conversation.

00:01:09.862 --> 00:01:13.115
- It's very important for us to
give this story justice

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:15.993
so that everyone who sees it
will be very moved,

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.411
and hopefully changed.

